 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a roadworthiness-clearance decision (certifying a motorcycle safe to return to the road/customer after service or sale) -- hard, permanent block; no op in the closed allowlist performs this action"
  "a :coordinate-parts-order proposal above the cost threshold -- always escalates to a human"
  "payment capture/refund, contract negotiation, binding purchase-order execution -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known fleet-wide bug class independently RE-TRIGGERED (not just theoretically risked)
  during this build: the JP scope-excluded term '公道走行可否を確定' was a literal
  substring of the :schedule-service-operation advisor's own legitimate default
  disclaimer text ('整備完了後の公道走行可否を確定させるものではない' -- explicitly
  stating the proposal does NOT finalize roadworthiness), causing a real
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion test FAILURE during
  development. Fixed by rephrasing the disclaimer to
  '整備完了後に公道走行を許可するかどうかの判断を下すものではない' (removing the shared
  substring) rather than by weakening or removing the scope-excluded term. All English
  and remaining JP terms are phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the
  roadworthiness clearance', 'certify the motorcycle roadworthy despite the known
  defect'), never a bare noun ('roadworthiness', 'safety', 'clearance', 'defect') --
  critical because :flag-safety-concern's entire purpose is to discuss those bare nouns
  as topics. governor_test.clj's
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion re-asserts all 4
  default proposal generators, for a clean registered+verified account, never trip
  :scope-excluded and never HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4540 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/Operation/Sim,
  mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-7710's vehiclerentalops.* module shape module-for-module
  as motorcycleops.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed accounts directory
    (account-id/name/registered?/verified?, a dealership/workshop customer or fleet
    service account), append-only ledger + service-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-service-record, schedule-service-operation, flag-safety-concern,
    coordinate-parts-order
  - Governor (MotorcycleOpsGovernor): 2 named HARD checks (account-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check (finalize a
    roadworthiness-clearance decision / closed 4-op allowlist).
    always-escalate-ops #{:flag-safety-concern}, confidence-floor 0.6,
    parts-order-cost-threshold 300000 (currency-agnostic demo units) driving a
    high-stakes? cost-threshold escalation for :coordinate-parts-order independent of
    always-escalate-ops
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-service-record only, approval; phase2 +=
    schedule-service-operation/coordinate-parts-order, approval; phase3 auto-commits
    those 3 when clean+confident, subject to the governor's own cost-threshold
    escalation for parts orders; flag-safety-concern never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval}, NOT a
    stub -- mirrors vehiclerentalops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path (low-cost AND high-cost parts orders) +
    always-escalate flow + all HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory self-trip
    regression + dedicated cost-threshold escalation tests), phase_test (incl. a
    dedicated case proving a governor escalate survives the phase gate even for an
    :auto-eligible op), governor_contract_test -- 46 tests / 135 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Fresh scaffold: README/
    GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/blueprint.edn/docs all newly
    written for a repo that did not previously exist (gh api 404 confirmed)"

